WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.588
Here are Part 2's three gates on one page.

2
00:00:02.588 --> 00:00:07.513
Actuation is done when each lane acts
through a connector or a declared exception,

3
00:00:07.513 --> 00:00:11.787
under a service identity, with a change
record where its class needs one.

4
00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:15.725
It closes the third gap, and there's
no automated check for it yet.

5
00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:18.013
You'll run one task per lane by hand.

6
00:00:18.013 --> 00:00:21.418
The re-read gate is done
when nothing closes without

7
00:00:21.418 --> 00:00:24.587
a re-read of the target,
which closes the first gap.

8
00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:26.699
The kit's tests prove its logic.

9
00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:29.664
The tempo gate is done when
the windows are measured,

10
00:00:29.664 --> 00:00:34.350
the identity fixes run through the loop,
and the evidence is produced on a schedule.

11
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.562
Two rules run through all three.

12
00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:40.825
A person's role stops at approval,
except for declared exceptions.

13
00:00:40.825 --> 00:00:43.562
And a success response
doesn't count as closure.

14
00:00:43.562 --> 00:00:48.537
The kit's first pass doesn't write to
Entra ID, Active Directory or SailPoint,

15
00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:52.610
which is why the actuation gate
relies on a manual lab for now.
